<title>USA: LaBarge wins $12.4-million supply contract.</title>
<headline>LaBarge wins $12.4-million supply contract.</headline>
<dateline>ST. LOUIS 1997-03-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>LaBarge Inc said Monday it received a two-year contract to produce electronic assemblies for the U.S. Navy's AEGIS weapon system being built by Lockheed Martin Corp.</p>
<p>The $12.4-million contract calls for LaBarge to produce printed circuit card assemblies and electronic modules at its Huntsville, Arkansas, manufacturing facility, the company said.</p>
<p>LaBarge designs and makes custom electronic products for the telecommunications, geophysical, medical, aerospace and defense markets.</p>
<p>Its shares were unchanged Monday at 5-7/8.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
